p=root/paths[3];s=p.read_text();anchor='- Primitive zero-argument';assert s.count(anchor)==1;s=s.replace(anchor,'- Native `number.toFixed(fractionDigits?: int)`, `number.toExponential(fractionDigits?: int)` and `number.toPrecision(precision?: int)` return UTF-8 strings through standard Rust formatting. Fraction digits range from 0–100; significant precision ranges from 1–100. Strict number receivers and integer arguments evaluate once in order; range failures preserve source locations. Halfway rounding follows Rust ties-to-even, with documented native shortest-digit choices. Standard String buffers avoid intermediate result allocations. [Milestone 74](../../docs/milestones/74-number-decimal-formatting.md) covers contexts, editor support, disposal and six shared-domain comparisons. Floating arbitrary-radix `toString` remains pending.\n'+anchor,1);p.write_text(s)
